{"study_accession":"PRJNA646740","secondary_study_accession":"SRP272279","title":"Most primitive Human Hematopoietic Stem Cell Populations","description":"Transcriptomic profiling (RNA-seq) of the four most primitive human stem and progenitor populations. Purpose: to compare the transcriptomic profile of the four most primitive human stem and progenitor populations (all are CD34+CD38-CD45RA-): CD90+CD49f+, CD90-CD49f+, CD90+CD49f-, CD90-CD49f-. Conclusions: previouls study of gene expression analysis of these populations were performed using microarray hence, this study represents the first analysis of transcriptomes from these populations generated by RNA-seq technology. The optimized data analysis workflows reported here should provide a framework for comparative investigations of expression profiles of other human blood stem/progenitor populations. Overall design: Methods: cells were obtained from human cord-blood and flow-sorted using the surface antigens described. 3 biological replicates/ population were used to extract total RNA and quality was verified (RIN >8). Libraries were prepared using with 20-25 ng/sample of starting RNA.","pubmed":"35440586","geo_series":"","n_samples":12,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN15559372","study_accession":"PRJNA646740","blood_class":"cord_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"CD90+CD49f+ S1 [NGS-6728]","description":"CD90+CD49f+ S1 [NGS-6728]","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM4674998","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":2,"first_public":"2021-07-04","attributes":[["source_name","CD90+CD49f+"],["age","post-natal"],["cell_type","cord blood CD34+ cells"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR12242170","experiment_accession":"SRX8750466","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2500","read_count":30542325,"base_count":6169549650,"first_public":"2021-07-04","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 2500 sequencing: GSM4674998: CD90+CD49f+ S1 [NGS-6728] Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"},{"run_accession":"SRR12242